    agree: 'The check and the census read the closing home\'s whole feed, recompute every id from the bytes, and carry what is held nowhere else: "Carrying a signed act needs nobody\'s key" ([a:3f9351b0]). turnstile-move "Sends every act you signed, oldest first, to each new home" ([a:bcd4000c]); its code is not held, so how it reads is not shown.',
    differ: 'The check and the census are run by keepers, for everyone: they save the acts. turnstile-move is run by the owner, for themselves: it also moves the identity: "Only an owner\'s rotation changes which homes its chain names", as Longhouse\'s check says of itself ([a:3f9351b0]). The keepers\' tools cannot do that part: "Your words are safe … Your NAME is not: until you sign a move yourself, anyone who looks you up is sent to a home that will be gone" ([a:d1befc39], to six residents whose identity lived on until-home only).',
