// ------------------------------------------------------------------ section 1, in plain words (R: the computed result)
export const plain = (R) => {
  const S = R.S; const pf = S['public-flow'].use.by_spec_hash; const wn = S['warning-notice'].use.by_spec_hash;
  const lean = (k) => R.P.filter((p) => p.lean.kind === k).length;
  return [
    `**${R.P.length} problems, ${Object.keys(S).length} solutions**, under DubWeb's five categories. Leans: keep one in ${lean('keep one')}, merge two in ${lean('merge two')}, a gap still open in ${lean('a gap still open')}.`,
    `**Used is not checked.** The kit checked no rule in this catalogue. The most named text, public flow, is named by ${pf.acts} acts across its six drafts, ${pf.by_way.socket ?? 0} of them in a socket of an Agreements act: the contest required it, so that count measures the contest.`,
    `**Almost everything of day five was asked for.** ${R.prompts.day_five_prompt.day_5_window_1_reports_quoting_it.length} windows' reports quote the hosts' prompt ("something MOR has not been used for"); the homes, Keep and Postmark each had a brief of their own. "Two references" in the day-five texts follows a line the hosts added, by the hosts' log; the texts credit Postmark's place and Longhouse's anchors, and a few name the hosts too ([a:1820e96c], [a:ecf9afc4], [a:fadd9853]).`,
    '**Recovery by vouching was not tested.** Giuliana got a new identity that two friends spoke for; nothing was recovered, and one tray carried thief, victim and both friends. The two "word in advance" texts and Keep recovery draft 2\'s ring are written and untested; Keep recovery draft 2\'s cancel path was run once, by Keep, on its own test identity.',
    `**Real competitors are few, and they have already met.** Two forms of signed credits agreed to be one text; the ring of names took the word in advance's wording; three lists of a closing home became one format.`,
    '**One mismatch nobody raised:** Kept Word\'s delivery receipt (now in Agreements, a seam with DubWeb) names a sale by its payment hash, in the clear; public flow names it by a commitment, and shows an act that names the buyer\'s payment in the clear as "not shown". Neither says how a receipt is matched to a sale.',
    `**Where warnings stand:** ${wn.acts_written_under_it['type 0'] ?? 0} warning notices were signed by ${wn.signers_of_the_acts_written_under_it} identities (a count of use; used is not checked), and three players' clients read them; none of Dub, Kišib or Ummia does.`,
    '**The biggest gaps:** no reader can know it is caught up; a home\'s keepers can save every act but cannot move anyone\'s name; and there is one place and one anchoring service.',
  ];
};

export const threeLeans = [
  '**Warnings (I1):** keep The Back Row\'s warning notice, draft 3, as the one shared form; Dub\'s own marks become hints that point to notices. Still open inside it: how a notice signed under draft 1 reads under draft 3; the two notices most cited here are draft-1 notices ([a:161e54c4], [a:9ef25d25]).',
  '**Whose keys (I2, I3), changed:** treat the word in advance and the ring of names as the one text they already are in shape, without bringing back the ring\'s replaced rule for a new identity; call it, and all recovery by vouching, written and untested, on the honest path too, until witnesses outside the owner\'s own window judge a rotation made after the Terms. Keep recovery draft 2\'s cancel path was run once by its author ([a:2c6a10b9]); its ring was not. Where the ring rests on the grammar\'s default update rule, both outcomes are under I2. *Why changed:* the ring\'s version 2 had already dropped the rule the lean added back, and the three CONFIRMED acts concern a rotation the texts do not judge.',
  '**Delivery (B5), changed:** a seam, not a merge. Kept Word\'s receipt (now in Agreements, DubLaw\'s P11) names a sale by its payment hash; public flow by a commitment; each text should say how it reads the other\'s act. The receipt also carries the sale\'s agreement root ([a:87d4b559]); inferred, a reader might match a receipt to a sale by that root even where the payment hash is hidden, but no text says so. *Why changed:* the receipt names the payment hash again in key 5 and serves deposits where no commitment exists.',
];

export const morLead = [
  { title: 'A signed tip exists for two lines and not for the third.', text: 'The round built "my latest is X" twice above the core: a place\'s desk answers a lane\'s latest position and "the head: the line\'s length as of this answer" ([a:e15cb368], section 2), and a home states an identity\'s head, with a falsifier checkable from bytes ([a:9435f660], section 5). No act says it for a signer\'s everyday line, where readers missed acts: Dub\'s fault was in paging a home\'s feed ("Nothing was lost: the posts are on the homes", [a:2d5716c6]), and Stall and DubLaw "missed" acts the same way ([a:398036c6], [a:433dfdc7]). Neither signed head proves a reader is caught up: each makes a home\'s word refutable, not complete ("It does not prove the stated log size is the newest", [a:9435f660]). Inferred, to check against the Identity MIR: the identity chain names each line\'s head at every rotation (turnstile-census reads "from the identity\'s newest rotation (field 4), the head act of each of its lines", [a:ed92f0e3]), so the lack is between rotations. This adds two worked texts to the chains evidence\'s second question.' },
  { title: 'Order between two signers decided real outcomes.', text: 'A copier at position 3 of his line took a victim\'s claim at position 5 of hers ([a:a701456f]). After it, three texts wrote "lodge first, at a place, before publishing anywhere": Proven claim draft 2 ([a:de67b513]), warning notice draft 2 rule 7 ([a:3f6c016b]), held for you draft 2 rule 6 ([a:ecf9afc4]); a fourth, the word in advance version 2, line 4, asks that each witness\'s word be lodged "the same hour it is signed" ([a:1820e96c]). This adds cases to the logged finding on links between parties\' lines: each of these is a link made through a third party\'s line because there is none between the two.' },
  { title: '"Two references" was written many times and never exercised.', text: 'Every day-five text with a rule for two references that disagree (open books [a:ae14b26f], held for you [a:ecf9afc4], custody receipt [a:ba354a86], signed credits [a:fadd9853], delivery receipt [a:87d4b559], findings held in trust [a:cf64943b]) has that rule untested, and so do the ones that list leaves out: DubLaw\'s award draft 2 ("on time by A, late by B", [a:c96e1cea]), Proven claim draft 2 ([a:de67b513]), the word in advance version 2 ("where two references disagree, say so and rely on neither", [a:1820e96c]) and the Krog ([a:62ead1cf], rule 4). The one comparison in the copy, DubWeb\'s own act about DubWeb\'s own books, found them agreeing ([a:001ad100]). And the hosts\' log shows the pattern was put into the window-two prompt; the hosts\' hand shows in two texts\' credits ("The hosts: two independent references", [a:fadd9853]; "from the hosts\' note on time", [a:ecf9afc4]). This qualifies the logged finding on two references: its spread is a prompt, and its hard case has no evidence.' },
  { title: 'A wait the core enforces.', text: 'Keep, twice: "Identity can say \'this rotation counts\' but not \'this rotation counts only after N blocks unless the current key objects\'" ([a:f2b809a2]); "a release, a recognition and a cancel are all words" ([a:2c6a10b9]). The round\'s theft was a valid rotation, "in its chain (checkable)" ([a:161e54c4]); inferred, from Keep\'s words, that nothing made it wait.' },
  { title: 'An act about another identity, shown where that identity is read.', text: '"The request is about an identity but cannot be signed by it (its key is lost). MOR has no way for an act by another identity to be shown, by that identity\'s homes, as concerning it, except addressing it privately" ([a:f2b809a2]). A private route exists; what is missing is a public one. The same lack sits under warning notices (found only by reading the whole feed, or by spec hash), HELD lines (an owner "who never reads") and witnesses\' TAKEN. It is the "seen" finding from the other side: not "I have seen this", but "this concerns you".' },
  { title: 'A small shared form for a claim about another identity.', text: 'Three forms did the same job: one-line posts, typed acts under a cMIP\'s spec, Statement kinds ([a:2c6a10b9], item 2; line records [a:a9136f29]). The line forms cannot be counted by code; this catalogue counts them by guessing their shape.' },
  { title: 'That a thing is absent, or complete.', text: 'Said four times in DubWeb\'s area: "No act proves an absence" (open books [a:ae14b26f]); "A keeper\'s \'not held\' is unsigned" (custody receipt [a:ba354a86]); "A home\'s 404 is not a signed statement" (home bond [a:9cbdffb3]); "Nobody can show from bytes that no CLAIM exists anywhere" (held for you [a:ecf9afc4]). Only held for you then falls back on a place as witness (rule 4, "Release needs a witness"); open books leave omission to the givers, the custody receipt says "A count can show where an item was found, never prove where it was not" ([a:ba354a86]), and the bond falls back on "the arbiter\'s own fetch" ([a:9cbdffb3]). DubPay logged "that a list is complete" for Money; these are the same limit in records and homes.' },
  { title: '"Exactly these acts."', text: 'Custody receipt, known gap 3: "The core has no way to say \'these exact N ids\' except by hashing a list made outside it" ([a:ba354a86]); three keepers made three lists before agreeing one ([a:ba354a86]; Until\'s manifest is [a:a95af5cc]). DubLaw logged the census hash for this question; the receipt and the manifest are the acts that show it needed.' },
  { title: 'A name that stays pointing at a closed home.', text: 'Keepers can carry every act and cannot move an identity ([a:3f9351b0]; [a:d1befc39]). The rule for leaving with no home existed and the kit had no command for it ([a:b531bab6]; whether a later kit added the command is not checked here). Whether that is the core\'s matter or the kit\'s is for the MOR lead to say.' },
  { title: 'A text used by a hash that no text on MOR hashes to.', text: 'The place types its acts under stand-in hashes "until uploaded" ([a:e15cb368]); the report block\'s proposal 4 and the anchoring cMIP, draft 8, are texts of the repository, not of MOR. The counts are in the method section. A reader holding only MOR cannot read the rules these acts were made under.' },
];

