export const limits = (R) => {
  const i = R.inputs; const q = R.prompts.day_five_prompt;
  return [
    `**The inputs, as they stood at this run.** This is version 2, read from the shared inventory's version 2 (\`inventory-v2/\`), which applies DubPay's and DubLaw's slice checks (its \`changes.md\` lists every record that moved). It holds ${i.records} records, ${i.web_records} proposed for Web, ${i.web_records_to_settle} of them to settle; the merged feature list holds ${i.features ?? 0} features, ${i.features_to_settle ?? 0} to settle (that list was not corrected in this session). Every area is a proposal; each "to settle" is shown as the inventory gives it.`,
    `**Solutions the inventory places in another area** (${i.solutions_the_inventory_proposes_for_another_area.map((x) => x.solution + ': ' + x.area).join('; ') || 'none'}). Those in Money were placed there in version 1 and are now settled in Money by both checks; they stay catalogued here, as in version 1, for the problems they serve, and DubPay's catalogue holds them. Those in Agreements, the delivery receipt and Proven claim, moved there by DubLaw's check and DubWeb's concession: their entries here are pointers to DubLaw's catalogue (\`_team/dublaw/wave-3/results/F/catalogue-agreements.md\`), and the comparison DubWeb shows under B5 and R2 is kept, marked as a seam.`,
    `**What is catalogued beside the inventory's records.** ${i.carriers_here_that_are_not_inventory_records.length} acts are listed as a solution's texts though the inventory has no record for them: later versions of words, code posted as text, an instance of anchoring, Turnstile's editions. They are carriers of a solution, not specification texts. Web records of the inventory left out of this catalogue: ${i.web_records_not_catalogued.length}${i.web_records_not_catalogued.length ? ' (' + i.web_records_not_catalogued.map((t) => String(t.title).replace(/^# /, '').slice(0, 50)).join('; ') + ')' : ''}.`,
    `**Counts here and in the inventory differ by rule, not by error.** The inventory counts per text; this catalogue counts per solution, across its drafts, with each act once. Its "by act" counts short forms; here short forms are kept apart. Read each number with its own rule.`,
    `**How use is counted.** By spec hash: distinct public acts, other than the solution's own texts, that are written under the hash, hold it as 32 bytes in their payload (a socket on an Agreements act) or in refs, or quote all 64 characters in words. By act id: the same, for the text acts' ids. By name: acts whose words match the pattern shown. The three are kept apart and overlap. Short forms (\`xxxxxxxx…\`) are counted apart and never as use. Sealed and private acts were not opened (${R.stats.sealed_items_not_opened} sealed items, ${R.stats.private_acts_not_opened} private acts), so use inside them is invisible.`,
    `**Used is not checked,** once more: no count here says a rule was applied correctly. "Kit" in the tables is this session's reading of what the kit could check, from the texts' own words and the hosts' counts; the kit's code was not re-read rule by rule.`,
    `**Prompted or chosen.** Two marks are shown for each solution: this catalogue's, from what the copy shows, and the shared inventory's. They differ where session A read a report by hand as answering the day-five brief and this script found no quote of it; both are given so DubWeb can judge. Notices 7 and 8 are in \`_research/hosts/\`. The day-five prompt is not a file: ${q.day_5_window_1_reports_quoting_it.length} day-5-window-1 reports quote or paraphrase it (${q.day_5_window_1_reports_quoting_it.map((x) => x.window).join(', ')}); ${q.day_5_window_1_reports_not_quoting_it.length} do not. Four day-five briefs are files: ${Object.entries(R.prompts.day_five_briefs_in_from_the_hosts).map(([t, b]) => `"${t.replace(/^A brief for /, '')}" (${b.windows.join(', ')})`).join('; ')}. "Not shown" means the copy does not show a prompt for it, not that there was none: the public windows' prompts were given in the hosts' conversation.`,
    `**Hashes in use with no text on MOR** (acts written under each, from this script): ${R.textless.map((t) => `\`${t.hash.slice(0, 8)}…${t.hash.slice(-4)}\` ${t.acts} acts by ${t.signers} signer${t.signers === 1 ? '' : 's'} (${t.what}${t.stand_in_of ? '; it is the SHA-256 of the fixed string "' + t.stand_in_of + '", by this script' : ''})`).join('; ')}.`,
    '**Trays.** "Carried by one tray" comes from the postman\'s log: the tray that posted an act\'s exact bytes. It shows which window\'s folder carried an identity\'s acts. It is how this catalogue shows that thief, victim and vouchers, and each owner with their witnesses, were played inside one window.',
    `**What is reading, not counting.** Every "agree", "differ" and "why" is this session's reading of the texts, quoted by act. Every cited act was resolved by the script to one public act in the copy (${R.citations.resolved} of ${R.citations.cited}). ${R.citations.read_in_the_act} of them were read in the act itself, by session C or by session F (which opened every act a reread finding cites, and every act section 4 cites); the other ${R.citations.cited_as_another_source_cites_them} are cited as a text that credits them, the wave-2 scan or the merged feature list cites them, and were not opened one by one. The JSON marks each (\`citations.cited_but_not_read_in_the_act\`), so a checker can start there. Faults are those the texts credit, plus those found on the way; DubWeb's wave-2 inventory holds a longer list of keyword candidates that was not read through.`,
    '**Not done.** No app was run. No code of an app was re-read for this catalogue beyond what the wave-2 scan read. The grouping into problems is one reading; a text could sit elsewhere, and pointers mark where.',
    '**What version 2 corrected, and how.** Every finding of the three rereads (`_team/dubweb/wave-3/reread/`) was checked in the full copy, act by act, and applied or not; `corrections.md` gives one line per finding. Leans that changed carry a "changed" line. What session F found wrong and did not fold in is in `found-while-correcting.md`. No new problem, solution or text was added.',
    '**Nothing was opened, signed, sent or asked of any home.** Only `_research/` and `_team/` were read; only this folder was written. No key file was read.',
  ];
};

// Acts cited above that this session did not open one by one: they are cited as a text that credits them,
